  <name>FastDir</name>
  <summary>Find out what is using your disk space</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.enekocm7">
    <name>enekocm7</name>
  </developer>

  <description>
    <p>
      FastDir scans a drive or folder on every CPU core, then shows you exactly
      where the space went: a sortable directory tree, a per-extension and
      per-category breakdown, and a cushion-shaded treemap where every square is
      a file.
    </p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Fast parallel scanner with exclusions and hard-link awareness</li>
      <li>Treemap, directory tree and file-type breakdown that stay in sync</li>
      <li>Rename, move, trash or delete files without rescanning</li>
      <li>Duplicate finder, saved scans and scan comparison</li>
      <li>A headless command-line tool (fastdir-cli) with JSON and CSV output and an MCP server</li>
    </ul>
  </description>

